Actually, it goes to show how little the censors know about what they are
doing.  We lost alt.sex*, which includes alt.sexual.abuse.recovery.  We lost
alt.games* because, in the approximate words of the man who made the 
recommendation to remove them, 'people are gumming up the system playing games 
in there'.   We lost alt.flames* cause there is naughty language in there, and
we lost alt.binaries.pictures.fine.art.d, a discussion group, when they blocked
alt.binar*.

We can get any of these through gopher, but that means using more net to get
there, so by restricting these groups and forcing those who would like to read
them to go surfing the net, they actually gum up the net worse.  I'm not that
net literate as per what the resource use difference is between using our
usenet provider to read mail or gophering to another site elsewhere, but I
figure since we pay for the provider and not for someone elses university
computer we should get as much as possible from our provider before using
another machine....

Just another case of the blind leading the sited....right off of the cliff.
